WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.600
Hey youtubers it's Charlie, only two more
episodes of Game of Thrones this season. So

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.580
because we spend so much time during the hiatus
theorycrafting I wanted to do a bonus video

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.780
for my favorite prophecies. I'm only including
things that are put forth as prophecy, so

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.670
like if Tyrion suffered a wine induced nightmare
that he was forcibly married to The Mountain

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:25.630
as punishment for losing trial by combat,
it's not a real prophecy. There's over fifty

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:29.260
that I know of, but this will just be my TOP
5. So if you guys want I can always do a follow

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.800
up with a longer breakdown later this summer.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.410
Don't forget that the next round of the weekly
giveaway starts when I post my Episode 9 review

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:40.360
tonight. I pick a random subscriber from the
comments on that video. It's not a contest

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.280
or anything. It's just a way for me to say
thank you to you guys for being so awesome.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.039
For all the prophecies I'm including the character
that it's given to and when they learned it

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:55.360
in the books if anyone wants to read the whole
thing. Here we go Number 5 - Maggy The Frog

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:01.609
So Cersei casually mentions her name on the
show out of context. In the books Maggy was

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:05.660
a fortune teller in Lannisport that Cersei
visited when she was 10 with 2 of her childhood

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:10.119
friends during a tournament for King Aerys.

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:15.640
Maggy let Cersei ask 3 questions but gave
her four answers. She predicted who Cersei

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.900
would marry, Robert not Rhaegar who had actually
just been knighted, Rhaegar that is. He was

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.909
about 7 years older than Cersei.

00:01:21.909 --> 00:01:26.920
Maggy also predicted Cersei would be Queen,
but that a younger more beautiful queen would

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.650
come and cast down and take all she held dear.
The theories behind this are that the younger

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:36.700
queen is either Maergary or Daenerys. In the
books Maergary isn't supposed to be more beautiful

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.320
than Cersei but because of the Purple Wedding
and Cersei's suggestion that she marry Tommen

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.649
it's still a pretty even guess as to who the
younger more beautiful queen is.

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:50.060
Maggy then predicted the total number of living
children she and Robert would have, separately.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.149
She predicted the total number of Robert's
bastards. Remember there were a lot, and Gendry

00:01:54.149 --> 00:02:01.149
is still floating somewhere south of Dragonstone.
And the total number of Cersei's living children,

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:06.040
3. Remember she had a stillborn child with
Robert. Maggy didn't say she would lose a

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:12.140
child but she predicted the total number and
Her 3 plus Robert's bastards hit the number.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:17.150
I won't say what the total number of Robert's
bastards is just in case the show changes

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:18.010
something.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:22.650
There was one more big part that relates to
the Valonqar which is High Valyrian for little

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:27.730
brother. But I'm not going to include it in
this video just because I think it's kind

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.470
of spoilery.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:33.989
If you want to read the whole prophecy it's
in Feast for Crows pages 540 to 541.

00:02:33.989 --> 00:02:36.129
Number 4 - The Winged Snake

00:02:36.129 --> 00:02:40.910
This is one of Bran's visions at the end of
book 2. In it his eyes are clouded with smoke

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:45.519
and ash and he sees a winged snake breathing
a river of flame in the sky. Behind the cliffs

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:46.769
tall fires were eating the stars.

00:02:46.769 --> 00:02:51.860
Because of the timing most people interpret
the smoke and ash to be the burning of Winterfell.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:56.030
Like we see it burning in the opening credits
every week. As for the dragon, there's a couple

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:01.030
theories. The craziest is that there's a dragon
underneath Winterfell that has just laid dormant

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:05.390
forever and the destruction of winterfell
woke it. There are hot springs beneath winterfell,

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:07.480
so it's possible but not probable.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.879
The other theory is that the dragon is supporting
evidence of Jon Snow being a Targaryen. He's

00:03:11.879 --> 00:03:14.370
the dragon rising from Winterfell.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:19.760
It's open to interpretation, but as a tangent,
Jojen claims that visions can be wrong but

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.659
greensight is not. And Bran and Jojen both
have the power of greensight. Which implies

00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:28.980
that all of Bran's visions are much closer
to the truth than other characters.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.760
Of course Jojen could also be misinterpreting
the claim about greensight too.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:36.030
You can read this one in Book 2 page 699

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.190
Number 3 - Azor Ahai

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:42.049
This prophecy comes from Melisandre and is
always mentioned in the same sentence with

00:03:42.049 --> 00:03:48.720
the sword Lightbringer. But Azor and Lightbringer
are actually two separate prophecies.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.430
The Azor prophecy says that when the Red Star
Bleeds and Darkness Gathers Azor Ahai shall

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:58.120
be born again amidst Smoke and Salt. Azor
Ahai is the mythical champion of the Red God,

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.080
Melisandre believes that he or she will lead
the army of the Red God against the Great

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.319
Other and his host of white walkers.

00:04:03.319 --> 00:04:06.920
The Red Star is the comet, which the show
has done already but it was more of a visual.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:07.640
Characters don't talk a lot about astronomy.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:11.670
The Darkness Gathering is a reference to the
coming battle with the Great Other. Like the

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.439
Long Night, the last great battle with the
white walkers. I'll have a link to that video

00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:17.190
at the end of this if you want to learn more
about it.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.660
I mentioned that Melisandre tells Stannis
he is Azor Ahai because they are on Dragonstone,

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:27.139
the place of Smoke and Salt. But alternatively,
that person could be Daenerys who was literally

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:31.400
born as a child at Dragonstone.
For anyone that's not a book reader, Dragonstone

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:35.330
is the Westerosi based ancestral home of the
Targaryens. Their true ancestral home was

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.280
the Valyrian Freehold but you get the idea.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:42.770
The important thing to remember about Azor
Ahai is that the person has to be RE-Born.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:47.750
So if you want to think Daenerys is Azor Ahai,
you have to look at that scene from season

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:52.509
1 where she stepped into Drogo's funeral pyre
and emerged with the dragons. That was when

00:04:52.509 --> 00:04:57.130
the comet first appeared, she wept salt tears,
you get the smoke from Drogo's flames and

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:00.020
she was reborn as the mother of dragons.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:04.080
It doesn't mean she's Azor Ahai, but I think
it's a very strong case if you ever wanted

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.139
to argue it with your friends.

00:05:05.139 --> 00:05:09.060
If you want to read the passage it's in Book
3 page 289.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.210
Number 2 - Daughter of Death

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:18.210
This is another Daenerys prophecy that's super
long so I'm going to condense. The title of

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:25.190
the prophecy comes from a passage that reads
"mother of dragons, daughter of death..."

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:29.750
She has visions that represent the deaths
of all those close to her including her brother

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:36.090
Rhaegar and what his dying words were. Robert
killed him at the Ruby Ford in the Trident.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:40.039
We don't actually know what his last words
were, but the prophecy says that he whispered

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:44.710
a woman's name. The best theory being Lyanna
Stark's name. If Robert heard him say it,

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:48.190
it's not something he would have ever told
anyone. Since he was in love with Lyanna himself.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:53.650
Daenerys then has a vision of Lightbringer,
the mythical flaming sword of Azor Ahai but

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:58.449
it was being held by a blue eyed king that
cast no shadow. Yes it sounds a lot like the

00:05:58.449 --> 00:06:02.610
white walker we saw at the end of episode
4. But the stronger theory I think is that

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:06.569
it represented the shadow baby that killed
Renly, since that was happening around the

00:06:06.569 --> 00:06:08.729
same time Daenerys had these visions.

00:06:08.729 --> 00:06:13.800
It also suggests that Daenerys and Stannis
might meet for better or worse at some point.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.039
There's a lot of potential spoilery parts
to her visions that relate to the Mummer's

00:06:17.039 --> 00:06:20.900
Dragon and the Stone Dragon so I'm going to
skip over those parts. Please if you're a

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.780
book reader use the spoiler tag if you want
to talk about it in the comments.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.660
But the rest of her visions are a mixture
of things that might have happened had her

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:31.509
child Rhaego lived and things that we've seen
happen. Like the liberation of her army in

00:06:31.509 --> 00:06:32.520
Yunkai.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:36.180
The whole prophecy is a collection of like
17 different passages that deal with stuff

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:38.539
from Book 1 to potentially the end of the
series. Visions could always be things that

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:41.180
we haven't seen in the books yet. So if you
do want to read the whole thing be careful

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:47.750
for potential spoilers. But it's in Book 2
pages 515 to 516, my final one is also part

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.130
of this House of the Undying epic montage.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:54.539
and my Number 1 favorite Prophecy - The Dragon
Has 3 Heads

00:06:54.539 --> 00:06:58.610
A lot of people refer to this as the 3 heads
of the Dragon as if they're three different

00:06:58.610 --> 00:06:59.349
characters.

00:06:59.349 --> 00:07:05.289
One of the rooms Daenerys sees in her visions
is of Rhaegar and Elia of Dorne with a newborn

00:07:05.289 --> 00:07:12.289
baby Aegon. The one the Mountain is supposed
to have killed. She learns that Rhaegar believed

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:19.370
that his children were the fulfilment of the
Azor Ahai prophecy, and in Daenerys vision

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:28.090
Elia asks Rheagar to play a song and he says
this is the "prince who was promised", "and

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.750
his is a song of ice and fire."

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:36.250
he turned, looked at Daenerys and said, "there
must be one more." "The Dragon has three heads".

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:42.889
Rhaegar was naming his children after Aegon
the conqueror, Elia was pregnant with Rhaenys

00:07:42.889 --> 00:07:47.690
when she was killed by the mountain. Implying
that Rhaegar intended to have one more baby

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:48.289
girl at a future date.

00:07:48.289 --> 00:07:49.900
So the 3 heads of the Dragon is really just
one piece of the fulfilment of the Azor Ahai

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:49.919
prophecy.

00:07:49.919 --> 00:07:52.919
But that doesn't mean Rhaegar's dead children
were the 3 heads of the dragon. George RR

00:07:52.919 --> 00:07:57.780
Martin has said that the three heads of the
Dragon need not all be Targaryens.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:04.000
But a lot of people, myself included, think
that Martin is just speaking cleverly without

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:09.300
lying. Meaning that there are characters alive
on the show that belong to other houses that

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.729
don't know they're Targaryens.

00:08:11.729 --> 00:08:16.539
If anything is clear on Game of Thrones, it's
that even highborn people sleep around.

00:08:16.539 --> 00:08:21.099
Jon Snow is the most famous theorized Targaryen,
but I don't want to name the other one just

00:08:21.099 --> 00:08:22.690
because I haven't seen any of you guys comment
on them so I don't want to spoil the surprise

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:23.090
if it comes true.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:25.449
But if you do want to comment on who you think
the three heads of the dragon are. Just use

00:08:25.449 --> 00:08:30.569
the spoiler tag. In my opinion, it's one of
the most popular things to theorycraft in

00:08:30.569 --> 00:08:31.199
the fandom.

